                                "sense_id": "ebc8e755-fbcf-33f0-98f5-65c0ea48cf84",
                                "text": "Proust's memory of a sweet crumb leads to the redemption of time; Gass's history as the history of things leads to the decay of a discandied world. Kohler presents a tour de force of memory in an account of a childhood candy shop; but, whatever beauty follows is contaminated by his anti-Semitism toward the store's owners."
